===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|demus||uncertain}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*dem-}}
For {{inh|la|itc-pro|*domos}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*dṓm|t=house, home}}, from root {{m|ine-pro|*dem-|t=to build}}. Cognates include {{cog|grc|δόμος}}, {{cog|sq|dhomë|t=a chamber, a room}}, {{cog|ae|𐬛𐬀𐬨|𐬛𐬀𐬨-}} {{cog|sa|दम|tr=dáma}}, {{cog|sla-pro|*domъ}} and further to {{cog|en|timber}}. At least indirectly cognate to {{cog|la|dominus}}.

The feminine gender is probably due to the original root noun; attempts to transfer it to the 4th declension are due to 2nd declension feminines being unusual outside of tree names. Some manuscripts of Plautus show forms in ''dem-''; De Vaan (2008) doubts their authenticity.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|domus}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|domus<irreg>|g=f}}

# [[house]], [[home]] {{gl|the building where a person lives}}
#: {{hyper|la|aedificium|aedēs}}
#: {{hypo|la|casa|domuncula|tugurium|gurgustium}}
#: {{uxi|la|Deō '''domuī'''que|For God and for '''home''' (motto of {{w|Methodist Ladies' College, Melbourne}})}}
#: {{uxi|la|Stet fortūna '''domūs'''|Let the good fortune of the '''house''' stand (motto of {{w|Harrow School}}, England)}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|2|792|quote=nox erat et tōta lūmina nūlla '''domō'''|trans=It was night, and [there were] no lights '''in''' the whole '''house'''.}}
## a [[townhouse]]
# any [[dwelling-place]] or [[abode]] {{gl|of people or animals}}
#: {{syn|la|domicilium|habitāculum|habitātiō|tēctum|mānsiō|sēdēs|aedēs}}
# the place of one's [[birth]] or [[residence]], [[native]] [[country]], [[town]]
#: {{hyper|la|patria}}
## {{gl|also of the [[shell]] of [[invertebrates]], [[tomb]]s of the dead}}
# [[household]], [[family]] {{gl|the dependants of the head of a house}}
## a group of [[disciple]]s, [[school]]; an intellectual [[movement]]
## {{lb|la|monarchy}} [[house]], [[dynasty]]
# {{lb|la|idiomatic}} one's own [[possession]]s or [[resource]]s
#: {{uxi|la|'''domum''' trahere|to drag '''into one's pocket'''}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''Domī''' versūra fit.|One is '''one's own''' [[creditor]]. {{q|proverb}}}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''domō''' afferre|to conceive '''on one's own'''}}
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Amphitryon|637|quote=id nunc experior '''domō'''|t=Now I'm learning this '''first-hand.'''}}
# {{lb|la|in [[locative case]] in phrases|idiomatic}} [[peace]]
#: {{uxi|la|bellī '''domī'''que; bellō '''domī'''que; vel bellī vel '''domī'''; '''domī''' bellōque; '''domī''' mīlitiaeque|t=in war and '''peace'''}}
#* {{Q|la|Titus Livius|Ab urbe condita|1|38|quote=ut non quietior populus '''domi''' esset quam militiae|t=so that the people should not become lazier '''in the time of peace''' than that of war}}

====Usage notes====
* This is one of a handful of common nouns that take the [[locative case]]; others are {{m|la|bellum}}, {{m|la|rūs}} and {{m|la|humus}}.
* It is irregular in that it has a mix of second and fourth declension forms, the second declension forms being more idiomatic. The classically most common declension is as follows:
:: ''domus, domūs, domuī, domum, domō — domūs, domōrum, domibus, domōs, domibus''.

